      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is indeed a horrific event, though a VRC protest would do literally NOTHING, not much different from real life protests most of the time.\nIf you want to actually help, there's many different ways to do so but this just isn't one of them.\nNot only would this be an event that causes even more fear in peoples minds, it would also very likely lead to an extremely chaotic session.\nTargeted attacks do happen in VRChat, and this would most likely be a very big target.\nYou mentioned you being a part of the VRC community for only 3 months, so I do understand why you'd think this is a thing you could do without major issues, though sadly that probably isn't actually the case.\nI've been a part of this community for a very long time and have seen things here that I wouldn't wish even my enemies to see.\nSome of those things include videos of *a bad group* in the middle of *doing very bad things to* someone, ruining the experience for entire lobbies.\nI do not want this to happen amongst people who probably already have seen some things they regret watching on Twitter.\nYou have good intentions, but this is not a good idea at all.\nToo sensitive of a topic, in a place it really does not belong and it would be too risky.",
